{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug final repair report.\n\nProblem: no-impact closes scanned every historical commit reference before learning that landing enforcement was out of scope.\n\nProven root cause/proof: `_check_work_landed` called `_referencing_commits` unconditionally (`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:219` before repair); the later `_check_file_impact_vs_diff` already returned for an empty accepted ticket/descendant impact union (`:283-285`). The report’s captured stack in `resolve_ticket_id -> _scan_alias -> json.load` matches that full-history loop. Empty union also makes the own-ticket impact check false, ruling out a lost enforcement result.\n\nTest: `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py::test_work_landed_skips_commit_discovery_when_scope_has_no_impact` was RED first because a sentinel observed `_referencing_commits`; the descendant-impact contrast was green. The test was removed from the fixer’s worktree, the held-out fixer changed production only, and the restored oracle was GREEN (2 passed). Reintroducing the exact unconditional-discovery defect returned the empty-scope oracle to RED while the descendant control remained green; restoring the fix returned 2/2 GREEN.\n\nFix: `_check_work_landed` now computes the existing `_union_file_impact(accepted_ids, tracker)` and returns before commit discovery only when it is empty. Nonempty own or descendant impact follows the unchanged discovery and enforcement path.\n\nScope/safety: the only production caller is the shared close precheck path (`close_precheck.py:635`). This restores the existing empty-union out-of-scope contract, adds no dependency or capability, and weakens no test. Relevant suite: 72 passed. `make lint`, `make typecheck`, complexity baseline, formatting, and `git diff --check` pass using the worktree venv.\n\nSibling sweep: construct search found no second unconditional full-history discovery in a no-impact close path. Parity rule: ticket close landing checks must skip commit discovery iff accepted-scope impact is empty. CLI (`_commands/transition.py:596`), library (`_lib_writes.py:228,299`), and MCP (`_mcp_writes.py:231`) converge on the same transition/close precheck; automated close callers use that shared core, and there is no dual-direction mirror operation. No MISSING surface.\n\nResidual risk/prevention: none observed beyond the separately tracked structured-output duplicate-candidate warning printed during plan review. The new mutation-proven regression prevents this scan ordering from returning.\n\nReplication: the original empty-scope production helper path now returns before a sentinel commit-history discovery, while a nonempty descendant scope still invokes discovery and diff enforcement."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787029441186422001,"uuid":"0ef93020-e3e4-4cc4-a36b-21cfae1a4422"}